WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.635
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Jake Tapper.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.505
I'm lucky enough to know
your wonderful wife, Jen.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have heard you say that
the character in this film -

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:11.077
in this book, excuse me --
Margaret, is based on Jen.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:14.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
How does she feel about that
if it is, in fact, true?

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:18.685 size:88% position:44%
-Well, I mean, Margaret
is loosely based on Jen.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.286 line:92%
She's a very strong feminist

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the moral center
of the family

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:26.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
and obviously gorgeous
and flawless.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.427 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, yeah.

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:30.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I think she feels
pretty good about it.

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have Margaret
have an interaction

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:35.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
with L. Ron Hubbard,
the founder of Scientology

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you have any hesitatio
about that,

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:41.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
as this is a famously litigiou
group of people?

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] I did.
I did. Absolutely.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:46.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then, I thought,
"So I feel no compunction

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.481
about writing about the Kennedys
and Sinatra and everything

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm gonna be afraid
of L. Ron Hubbard's ghost?

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.755 size:78% position:39%
I mean, so, you know,
I thought about it.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:59.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, should I call it, like
the Church of Biology?

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.060 line:92%
But then I'm like, "Why? Why?"

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm writing about
everybody else that's real

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:04.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm gonna blink
with this one group?

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's fiction. It's fiction
You know?

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:09.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
And just for the record
so the lawyers don't have to -

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't have L. Ron Hubbar
kill anybody.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:15.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just so everybody knows.
So everybody knows.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sounds like you're still
going to get a call.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:21.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey. I can't believe
we've never talked about this.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.115 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Some of your film work.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:24.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've been on this show
over a dozen times.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:27.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a film
I love a great deal.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Doug Liman film
"Edge of Tomorrow."

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have a cameo.
I want to show it real quick

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:37.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then hear how you enjoye
this bit of acting work.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.465 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.400 line:92%
-The only thing missing is you

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.868 line:92%
-She killed hundreds of mimics

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.104 size:78% position:39%
-She was able to kill
hundreds of mimics

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.505 line:92%
on only her first day in combat.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:48.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
Imagine an army
of Rita Vrataskis.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:51.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So there you go.
Tom Cruise on your show.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.713 line:92%
How was he to work with, Jake?

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:57.283
-You know, they -- I didn'
even know he was in the movi

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
until, like, a day
before it came out.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:03.189 line:92%
They CGI'd him into my set

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't get to meet --
When Wolf --

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.594 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Wolf did a cameo on,

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.996 size:88% position:44%
I think, the most recent
"Mission: Impossible."

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:11.364 size:88% position:44% line:92%
They flew him to London.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:14.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
They put him up first-class.
He was in a scene.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
He has photos of him
and Tom Cruise together.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
But for me,
they just did a CGI thing.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:20.640 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I don't even think --

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't even think
I got a dollar from that.

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:25.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughter ]
-I don't think I got --

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
By the way, it's a good --
it's a good movie.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:30.450
And I am -- Is this becaus
of the Church of Scientology

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you brought that up?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.520 size:84% position:42%
That's why he was like,
"This guy's gonna put

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.755
L. Ron Hubbard in a book.
I want no part of him."

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:38.191
-That's why he CGI'd it? Because
he knew that was gonna --

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:41.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because "Edge of Tomorrow,
he knows the future.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.729 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Okay. Makes sense.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:45.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I always --
I thought Wolf Blitzer

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:48.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
was great in the
"Mission: Impossible" movies

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:49.569 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It bums me out.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
My least favorite thing
about the "Mission: Impossible

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:55.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
movies is that
they don't just put --

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:58.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would so prefer
to see what Simon Pegg

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:01.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
looked like
in a Wolf Blitzer mask.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:04.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
Instead of that move of, like,
it's clearly Wolf Blitzer,

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:05.285 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and then he does this.

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:08.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just, like, make
the most hyper-realistic -

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:11.057 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It would look so bad.

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:12.258 line:92%
And that would be more fun

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It would look like when
Sudeikis would do Wolf Blitzer

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:18.064
When it looked and sounded
nothing like Wolf Blitzer.

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:22.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How dare you.
Sudeikis would take weeks!

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:25.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
If he was doing a Wolf Blitzer
he'd go away to his cabin.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:29.275
-He went to Buffalo. I know.
-He would just wear headphones

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know how he got it wrong?
You know how he got it --

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
First of all, I love Sudeikis,
so let me just say

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
that even though
I'm not a fan of his Blitzer

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a fan of everything else
he does.

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:38.218 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But the beard --

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:41.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is really a costume
design and beard and makeup.

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:44.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
You never had the beard
shorn enough.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.593 line:92%
He has a very close shave.

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:49.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's assiduous
with the grooming.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:52.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the Sudeikis Wolf,
it was too shaggy.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:54.534
It was like -- Honestly,
it was like a Kenny Rogers

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:58.838
-Wolf -- is it true he shave
during commercials, right?

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.540 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean,
he doesn't do it himself.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
He has people.
-Right. He has a team.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
By the way, I thought
you needed to be worried

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:09.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
about Scientologists
coming after you,

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:14.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
but when the "SNL"
beard department sees this

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.655 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
lock your doors.

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, um,
here's my last question.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:20.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think, you know,
because you have a family...

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:23.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you are not
the first best-selling author.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:26.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your daughter, Alice,
wrote a book.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
Best-seller --
"Raise Your Hand."

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:31.004
Does she have any fear tha
you're going to overtake her

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:31.904 line:92%
or does she just sort of scoff

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:34.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the fact that
you're second to the party

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.076 line:92%
-[ Laughs ] I am the last

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the totem pole
of the Tapper family.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:41.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't know
where you are in yours,

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:44.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, like, I am
underneath the dogs.

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:48.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know, Alice
isn't even looking down at me.

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:49.856 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I mean, like, I'm --

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:51.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's like looking
at the Kansas City Royals.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure. Sure.
-Last place.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
She actually has an idea
for another one,

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:59.365 line:92%
but the problem is she's 13 now,

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:02.235 size:88% position:44%
so she's got other stuff
she wants to do, so --

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.369 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Right. It was very--

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:06.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it just speaks
to her being ahead of the game

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:09.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little bit
that she wrote a book at a tim

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:12.245
when she was at the age
to have the focus for it.

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:13.646 line:92%
-[ Laughs ] Yeah, exactly.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm going to do it now
when I'm 11

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:20.019
because I've got other stuff t
do as a teen and as an adult."

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:23.056 size:81% position:41%
-Right. She'll work on
the movie adaptation

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:24.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
of "Raise Your Hand"
when she's 13.

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:27.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
She doesn't have time
to go write another book.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.028 line:92%
Hey, buddy, congratulations.

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always a delight
to see you.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.965
Hopefully next time you'll
be here in person with us.

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:35.234 size:88% position:44%
-Absolutely. Absolutely.
-"The Devil May Dance"

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
is available
wherever books are sold,

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:40.573
but please support your loca
and independent bookstores

